# Commits that changed only how something is written, never what it says.
#
# `git blame` attributes a line to whatever commit last touched it, so a
# repo-wide mechanical pass buries the real authorship of every line it edits.
# Listing that commit here makes blame skip it and report the commit that
# actually wrote the line.
#
# `scripts/check_dates.py` depends on this: it compares each date stamp against
# the commit that wrote it, and without this file the commit that CORRECTED the
# dates would look like the commit that drifted them.
#
# For your own `git blame`, either pass --ignore-revs-file=.git-blame-ignore-revs
# or set it once:
#
#     git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs
#
# Add a commit here only if it is a pure mechanical rewrite. A commit that
# changes meaning must stay visible in blame.

